Partition blank emulated SSDs

fdisk rejects a first sector of 32 ("Value out of range", the minimum is
2048 with 1 MiB alignment), so the partition table is never written. ECG
SSDs already have a partition 1, which mkfs then reformats, but the
emulated SSD starts out blank. Accept the default first sector instead,
and wait for udev to create the partition device rather than sleeping,
which may not be long enough under QEMU's emulation.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [QEMU only]
---
--- a/kepler-ssd-format.sh
+++ b/kepler-ssd-format.sh
@@ -69,13 +69,13 @@
         n   # Add a new partition
         p   # Make it a primary partition
         1   # Make it partition number 1.
-        32  # Start at sector 32
+        ""  # Blank line to accept the default first sector.
         ""  # Blank line to accept end of the device as the last sector.
         w   # Write changes
     )
 
     printf '%s\n' "${fdisk_cmds[@]}" | fdisk "${dev}" &>/dev/null
-    sleep 1
+    udevadm settle
     mkfs.ext4 -F -O 64bit "${dev_p1}" &>/dev/null
 }
 
